Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:38.840 --> 00:02:04.789 align:start position:0%
 
hey  everybody's good  all right we're good all right good  morning i'm lieutenant ray spencer i'm  the homicide lieutenant with the las  vegas metropolitan police department  i'm out here this morning to brief you  on a homicide investigation that we are  conducting in the 600 block of north  11th the details that i have right now  are very preliminary but at around seven  o'clock this morning  metro police received report that a male  had been shot after he had ran  to the front of a 7-eleven that was at  the intersection of bonanza in maryland  parkway  officers arrived that male was  transported to umc trauma where he was  pronounced deceased  he is a hispanic male in his late  twenties what we have learned from the  investigation is that the victim  was walking on 11th street which is  adjacent to the 7-11  when at some point there was an  altercation we do not know if he had an  altercation  with a person on foot or in a vehicle we  are still trying to determine that  we are in the process of canvassing the  area looking for witnesses and we are  also trying to locate any surveillance  video  i urge anybody who has any information  to reach out to crime stoppers  there's reward money available and you  can remain completely anonymous  or you can also reach out to homicide at  lvmpd.com  so again still very early on in the  investigation but i'll take a couple  questions if you have them  yes there was a store clerk there was a  citizen who immediately  rendered aid and along again with the  clerk there were two clerks inside  who called 9-1-1 prior to police  arriving so right now we have  the it's a community group called trauma  intervention program  they are out here providing assistance  to the clerk  obviously who was shaken up for what  they witnessed  the victim was shot on 11th street  basically behind the 7-eleven  so and i noticed that pecos was shut  down over at 95.  so the original details that there was  an incident on  in northeast in the northeast area off  of pecos that was thought  potentially was related we have ruled  that out as being related so at this  point we don't believe that has any ins  uh any involvement with us  well we do know that the victim was on  foot  prior to the shooting so we don't know  what  again led up to the shooting as far as  you know  why he was approached or who he  approached we just know he was shot  and then ran into the 7-eleven seeking  help  no there were no weapons found on the  victim  i don't have the specifics on that  still too early we're still trying to  figure out exactly why the victim was in  the area  still don't know so all right thank you  guys  uh we'll be out here probably for the  next couple out two to three hours  before it's opened up  all right thank you  making a movie over here not much to  look at  i'm out of ideas  um  all right we're good yeah all right good  morning i'm lieutenant ray spencer

